   <!-- ALL CHILDREN IN SCHOOL -->
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="mod" ss:MergeAcross="5"><Data ss:Type="String">13. All Children in School (ACiS)</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Students in Common Pool</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">COUNT(DISTINCT EMIS_ID) across both Common Pool exports (union on EMIS_ID): children who left universal data (TC issued) and are not yet back in a school.</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral (lower better)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed) · State 2,91,194 · Tile + grid</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Students surveyed</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">COUNT(children with Survey_Status = Surveyed in the roster, or present in the Surveyed report).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral (higher better)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed) · State 2,68,267 · Tile + grid</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Pending to be surveyed</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Students in Common Pool − Students surveyed.</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral (lower better)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed) · State 22,927 · Tile + grid</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Survey completion %</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">%</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Students surveyed ÷ Students in Common Pool × 100. Recomputed from the summed numerator and denominator at every scope (not an average of unit %).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Tile: range 50–100, higher better. Grid pill: &lt; 80 red · 80–95 amber · ≥ 95 green</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed) · State 92.1% · Tile + grid</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Students admitted to schools</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">COUNT(Admit_status = Admitted).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral (higher better)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed) · State 45,042 · Tile + grid</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Students to be admitted</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">COUNT(dropout_bucket = &quot;To be Admitted&quot;) in the Surveyed report.</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral (lower better)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed) · State 61,333 · Tile + grid</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Dropouts with reason recorded</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">COUNT(surveyed children with a dropout reason recorded).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed) · State 2,68,260 · Tile</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Dept. action taken</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">COUNT(surveyed children AND (Admitted OR umis_status = Joined_higher_edu OR owning department = &quot;No action — child deceased&quot;)). Owning department is a derived mapping from reason → sub-reason (e.g. ITI / Polytechnic → Higher &amp; Technical Education).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral (higher better)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed) · State 52,345 · Tile; Department action tab</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Dept. action to be taken</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Students surveyed − Dept. action taken.</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral (lower better)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed) · State 2,15,922 · Tile + grid</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Dropout rate %</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">%</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">N ÷ D × 100 over classes I–XII. N = common-pool children not re-enrolled (Admit_status ≠ Admitted) in the class / level; D = students enrolled in that class / level (2026-27 enrolment roll, grade-wise boys + girls). School type / gender / class filters narrow both N and D (CWSN / UMIS do not apply — the roll has neither).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Tile: range 0–5, lower better. Grid pill: ≥ 3 red · 1.5–3 amber · &lt; 1.5 green</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports + 2026-27 enrolment roll · State 2,46,152 ÷ 1,11,06,881 = 2.22% · Tile; Dropout rate tab</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Dropouts not re-enrolled</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Students in Common Pool − Students admitted to schools (children who left and are still out).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral (lower better)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports + 2026-27 enrolment roll · State 2,46,152 · Tile; Dropout rate tab</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Dropout rate — level-wise (view)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">%</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Same formula per level: Primary I–V · Upper Primary VI–VIII · Secondary IX–X · Hr. Secondary XI–XII. N = common-pool children not re-enrolled (Admit_status ≠ Admitted) in the class / level; D = students enrolled in that class / level (2026-27 enrolment roll, grade-wise boys + girls).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Pill as above</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports + 2026-27 enrolment roll · State Primary 1.84% · Upper Primary 0.99% · Secondary 5.65% · Hr. Sec 1.20% · Dropout rate tab</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Dropout rate — school type-wise (view)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">%</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Same formula per management group: Government (incl. Central Govt) / Fully Aided / Partially Aided / Private (Un-aided).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Pill as above</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports + 2026-27 enrolment roll · State Govt 2.72% · Fully Aided 2.25% · Partially Aided 2.66% · Private 1.78% · Dropout rate tab</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Reasons for dropout — grade-wise (view + chart)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Not-re-enrolled dropouts per class split into Migration (reason = Related to migration) · CWSN (reason = Welfare of differently-abled) · Illness (reason = Related to health) · Child marriage (sub-reason = Forced into child marriage) · Other · Not recorded (not surveyed yet).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports + 2026-27 enrolment roll · State Migration 56,502 · CWSN 3,322 · Illness 3,375 · Child marriage 71 · Other 1,60,750 · Not recorded 22,132 · Dropout rate tab; ACiS dashboard chart</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Dropout rate — grade-wise (chart)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">%</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Dropout rate % per class I–XII (tooltip shows N and D).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports + 2026-27 enrolment roll · ACiS dashboard chart</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Potential dropouts</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">COUNT(DISTINCT EMIS_ID) of enrolled students absent 15 or more days in the last 30 days (the PD report window).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral (lower better)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — EMIS Potential Dropout report (2026-09-01 → 2026-10-01) · State 29,075 · Tile + grid</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Potential dropout %</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">%</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Potential dropouts ÷ students enrolled in the school types the PD report covers (Government) × 100. School type / gender / class filters narrow both numerator and denominator (class uses the grade-wise roll).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Tile: range 0–5, lower better. Grid pill: ≥ 2 red · 1–2 amber · &lt; 1 green</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — EMIS Potential Dropout report (2026-09-01 → 2026-10-01) + enrolment roll · State 29,075 ÷ 40,36,861 = 0.72% · Tile + grid</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Potential dropout repeaters</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">COUNT(Red_Flag_Status = Repeater) — EMIS flag for students who appeared in the last two PD reports. (Not Repeater 7,159 · Not updated 14,107.)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral (lower better)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — EMIS Potential Dropout report (2026-09-01 → 2026-10-01) · State 7,809 · Tile + grid</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Potential dropout reasons</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Potential dropouts grouped by reason category (department) → dropout_reason; share = reason ÷ PD in scope. A reason of &quot;0&quot; / blank is shown as &quot;Not updated&quot; (14,107 statewide).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — EMIS Potential Dropout report (2026-09-01 → 2026-10-01) · View details: PD reasons tab</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Potential dropouts grade-wise</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Potential dropouts by class, split boys / girls and by reason category.</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — EMIS Potential Dropout report (2026-09-01 → 2026-10-01) · View details: PD grade-wise tab</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Dropout reasons (view)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Common-pool children grouped by reason → sub-reason; share = reason ÷ children with a reason; admitted back vs still out per reason.</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed) · View details: Dropout reasons tab</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Department action (view)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Per owning department: cases referred = surveyed children routed to it; action taken / to be taken as above; Action taken % = taken ÷ referred × 100.</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed) · View details: Department action tab</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Management-wise (chart)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Potential dropouts and common-pool students grouped by school type into Government (incl. Central Govt) / Fully Aided / Partially Aided / Private (Un-aided). PD is 100% Government (report covers govt schools only).</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed); Real — EMIS Potential Dropout report (2026-09-01 → 2026-10-01) · ACiS dashboard chart</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Grade-wise (chart)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Potential dropouts and common-pool students by class, stacked boys / girls.</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed); Real — EMIS Potential Dropout report (2026-09-01 → 2026-10-01) · ACiS dashboard chart</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">All Children in School</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">School category-wise (chart)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Count</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Common-pool students and potential dropouts by Primary / Middle / High / Hr. Secondary (School_Category); each on its own scale.</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Neutral</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Real — Common Pool reports (To be Surveyed ∪ Surveyed); Real — EMIS Potential Dropout report (2026-09-01 → 2026-10-01) · ACiS dashboard chart</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Filters</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell" ss:MergeAcross="4"><Data ss:Type="String">School type, gender and class apply to every ACiS figure. CWSN and UMIS status apply to common-pool (dropout) figures only — the PD report has no such fields.</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Drill-down</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell" ss:MergeAcross="4"><Data ss:Type="String">District → Block → School → students: common-pool children (survey / admit status, reason, sub-reason, department) and potential dropouts (reason, days absent, repeater status), as two separate lists.</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Removed (on request)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell" ss:MergeAcross="4"><Data ss:Type="String">TC dropouts from universal data · Students bridged and admitted · Avg bridging duration · To be validated by SMC.</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Not built (no source data)</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell" ss:MergeAcross="4"><Data ss:Type="String">Regularised (back 8+ days in 2 weeks) · PD duration (&lt; 1 wk / 1–2 / 2–4 / &gt; 4 wks) · Monthly PD trend since the start of the AY. All need several dated PD reports (or daily student attendance); only one PD report window (2026-09-01 → 2026-10-01) and 4 days of attendance exist. Dropout rate uses the 2026-27 roll as D (grade-wise enrolment for earlier years exists at state level only).</Data></Cell></Row>

   <Row></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Legend</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Orange italic rows = PLACEHOLDER KPI (shows "–" in the dashboard until the source field is connected).</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">RAG</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell" ss:MergeAcross="4"><Data ss:Type="String">For % KPIs: normalise value into its [lo,hi] range (invert if lower-is-better); score &gt;0.66 = green, &gt;0.33 = amber, else red. Count KPIs are neutral (no RAG cut-off invented).</Data></Cell></Row>
   <Row><Cell ss:StyleID="cell"><Data ss:Type="String">Scope aggregation</Data></Cell><Cell ss:StyleID="cell" ss:MergeAcross="4"><Data ss:Type="String">Percentages are student-weighted across the units in the current scope (State / District / Block); counts are summed.</Data></Cell></Row>
  </Table>
 </Worksheet>
</Workbook>
